window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/courses/b166-9a273500827946ab.json"]={sha256:"9a273500827946abe714182b60b3df4848d40278a586e041b37a140b643f97f3",value:{"id":"b166","title":"明挖覆蓋隧道施工","titleEn":"Cut-and-cover tunnel construction","category":"underground","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"本課以整合明挖隧道的地表界面、支撐、水壓與回填階段為主線，從開挖尺度與地表影響與側向土壓與變形條件建立系統邊界，再把箱體自重與施工抗浮、支撐拆換與荷載轉移連到地表恢復與地下資產交接。開挖、結構施工與回填具有不同荷載路徑，竣工模型不能取代施工模型。 十單元以可核算的模型和可追溯證據逐步判讀不同失效。","summaryEn":"This course focuses on integrate surface interfaces, bracing, water pressure and backfilling in cut-and-cover tunnels. It begins with Excavation scale and surface impact and Lateral soil pressure and movement conditions, links Box weight and temporary flotation and Brace removal and load transfer, and ends with Surface restoration and underground handover. Excavation, structural work and backfilling have different load paths; the final model does not replace staged models. Ten units use reproducible models and traceable evidence to distinguish failure mechanisms.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"ug-cutcover","subcategoryTitle":"明挖逆打與沉管","subcategoryTitleEn":"Cut-and-cover, top-down and immersed tunnels","learningTrack":"underground","learningSubdiscipline":"ug-cutcover","learningTags":["underground","ug-cutcover","excavation"],"architectureFamily":"excavation","architectureNodes":[["開挖尺度與地表影響","Excavation scale and surface impact"],["支撐軸力與溫度","Brace force and temperature"],["箱體自重與施工抗浮","Box weight and temporary flotation"],["支撐拆換與荷載轉移","Brace removal and load transfer"],["地表恢復與地下資產交接","Surface restoration and underground handover"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[0,3]],"diagram":{"type":"excavation","labels":["開挖尺度與地表影響","支撐軸力與溫度","箱體自重與施工抗浮","支撐拆換與荷載轉移","地表恢復與地下資產交接"],"labelsEn":["Excavation scale and surface impact","Brace force and temperature","Box weight and temporary flotation","Brace removal and load transfer","Surface restoration and underground handover"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"整合算例所有輸入均為教學假設。首先檢查開挖尺度與地表影響：V=L*B*H=100 m*14 m*8 m=11200 m3；再獨立檢查側向土壓與變形條件：resultant=0.5*Ka*gamma*H^2=0.5*0.33*18 kN/m3*(8 m)^2=190.1 kN/m。長 100 m、深 8 m，寬由 14 增為 16 m，土方由 11200 增為 12800 m3，增加 14.3%；支撐跨距及水力影響不只按體積同比放大。 兩個結果不能自動組成完整設計，因為開挖、結構施工與回填具有不同荷載路徑，竣工模型不能取代施工模型。 將將建物水準、傾斜與原有裂縫圖按結構跨間比較作為模型以外的驗證證據，並保留原始紀錄與尚待確認的邊界。","textEn":"All inputs in this integrated example are teaching assumptions. First check Excavation scale and surface impact: V=L*B*H=100 m*14 m*8 m=11200 m3. Independently check Lateral soil pressure and movement conditions: resultant=0.5*Ka*gamma*H^2=0.5*0.33*18 kN/m3*(8 m)^2=190.1 kN/m. At 100 m length and 8 m depth, widening from 14 to 16 m raises excavation from 11200 to 12800 m3, by 14.3%; brace spans and hydraulic effects do not merely scale with volume. The two results are not a complete design because excavation, structural work and backfilling have different load paths; the final model does not replace staged models. Use compare building levels, tilt and baseline cracks by structural bay as evidence independent of the calculation, retaining raw records and unverified boundaries.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":14,"enrichmentVersion":14,"stages":[{"id":"b166-v14-s1","title":"地層條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Ground conditions, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「開挖尺度與地表影響」與「側向土壓與變形條件」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Excavation scale and surface impact\" and \"Lateral soil pressure and movement conditions\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b166-v14-01","title":"開挖尺度與地表影響：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Excavation scale and surface impact: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「開挖尺度與地表影響」如何影響明挖覆蓋隧道施工的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Excavation scale and surface impact” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Cut-and-cover tunnel construction”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"明挖把地下結構施工直接連到地表交通、管線和鄰房，開挖寬度也改變支撐跨距與土體卸載。土方體積只是物流量級，不能代表所有變形風險；工法選擇應把永久箱體、臨時圍護和地表使用需求放在同一斷面。 判別這個機制時，應觀察比對探測管線、道路分期及開挖邊界的共同座標；若出現只按土方安排忽略管線支承，既有設施因卸載或位移受損，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「開挖尺度與地表影響」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Cut-and-cover directly couples underground construction to traffic, utilities and neighbours. Width changes brace spans and unloading as well as spoil volume. Volume describes logistics rather than all deformation risks; compare the permanent box, temporary retention and surface-use demands in one section. Use the following check to discriminate the mechanism: Compare detected utilities, road stages and excavation limits in shared coordinates. If a spoil-only plan misses utility support and damages services through unloading or movement, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Excavation scale and surface impact” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：V=L*B*H=100 m*14 m*8 m=11200 m3。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: V=L*B*H=100 m*14 m*8 m=11200 m3.","failure":"常見誤解：「土方體積相同就代表兩個明挖工程風險相同」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Equal excavation volume means identical risk for two cut-and-cover projects\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「開挖尺度與地表影響」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Excavation scale and surface impact”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b166-v14-01-k1","title":"開挖尺度與地表影響","titleEn":"Excavation scale and surface impact","text":"明挖把地下結構施工直接連到地表交通、管線和鄰房，開挖寬度也改變支撐跨距與土體卸載。土方體積只是物流量級，不能代表所有變形風險；工法選擇應把永久箱體、臨時圍護和地表使用需求放在同一斷面。","textEn":"Cut-and-cover directly couples underground construction to traffic, utilities and neighbours. Width changes brace spans and unloading as well as spoil volume.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]},{"id":"b166-v14-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：土方體積相同就代表兩個明挖工程風險相同 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Equal excavation volume means identical risk for two cut-and-cover projects Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「開挖尺度與地表影響」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Excavation scale and surface impact\" is correct?","options":["土方體積相同就代表兩個明挖工程風險相同","明挖把地下結構施工直接連到地表交通、管線和鄰房，開挖寬度也改變支撐跨距與土體卸載。","所有擋土牆都可以直接使用完全主動土壓"],"optionsEn":["Equal excavation volume means identical risk for two cut-and-cover projects","Cut-and-cover directly couples underground construction to traffic, utilities and neighbours.","Every retaining wall can directly use fully active earth pressure"],"answer":1,"explanation":"明挖把地下結構施工直接連到地表交通、管線和鄰房，開挖寬度也改變支撐跨距與土體卸載。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Cut-and-cover directly couples underground construction to traffic, utilities and neighbours. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b166-v14-02","title":"開挖尺度與地表影響：定量估算","titleEn":"Excavation scale and surface impact: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"],"prerequisiteIds":["b166-v14-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「開挖尺度與地表影響」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Excavation scale and surface impact” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：V=L*B*H=100 m*14 m*8 m=11200 m3。開挖、結構施工與回填具有不同荷載路徑，竣工模型不能取代施工模型。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: V=L*B*H=100 m*14 m*8 m=11200 m3. Excavation, structural work and backfilling have different load paths; the final model does not replace staged models. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比對探測管線、道路分期及開挖邊界的共同座標。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare detected utilities, road stages and excavation limits in shared coordinates.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b166-v14-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：V=L*B*H=100 m*14 m*8 m=11200 m3。開挖、結構施工與回填具有不同荷載路徑，竣工模型不能取代施工模型。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: V=L*B*H=100 m*14 m*8 m=11200 m3. Excavation, structural work and backfilling have different load paths; the final model does not replace staged models. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]},{"id":"b166-v14-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「開挖尺度與地表影響」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Excavation scale and surface impact\", which statement holds?","options":["基底往上動的所有原因都屬同一種失效","箱體牆面不裂就能保證所有穿牆位置都不漏","原創教學假設：V=L*B*H=100 m*14 m*8 m=11200 m3。"],"optionsEn":["Every cause of upward base movement is the same failure mechanism","Uncracked box walls guarantee every penetration remains watertight","Original teaching assumptions: V=L*B*H=100 m*14 m*8 m=11200 m3."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：V=L*B*H=100 m*14 m*8 m=11200 m3。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: V=L*B*H=100 m*14 m*8 m=11200 m3. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b166-v14-03","title":"開挖尺度與地表影響：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Excavation scale and surface impact: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"],"prerequisiteIds":["b166-v14-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「開挖尺度與地表影響」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Excavation scale and surface impact” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比對探測管線、道路分期及開挖邊界的共同座標。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「只按土方安排忽略管線支承，既有設施因卸載或位移受損」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare detected utilities, road stages and excavation limits in shared coordinates. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: A spoil-only plan misses utility support and damages services through unloading or movement. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將比對探測管線、道路分期及開挖邊界的共同座標列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現只按土方安排忽略管線支承，既有設施因卸載或位移受損，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","observationEn":"Site practice: Apply the following check at handover: Compare detected utilities, road stages and excavation limits in shared coordinates. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If a spoil-only plan misses utility support and damages services through unloading or movement, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","failure":"注意干擾：只按土方安排忽略管線支承，既有設施因卸載或位移受損。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A spoil-only plan misses utility support and damages services through unloading or movement. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b166-v14-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比對探測管線、道路分期及開挖邊界的共同座標。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「只按土方安排忽略管線支承，既有設施因卸載或位移受損」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。","textEn":"Compare detected utilities, road stages and excavation limits in shared coordinates. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: A spoil-only plan misses utility support and damages services through unloading or movement. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]},{"id":"b166-v14-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將比對探測管線、道路分期及開挖邊界的共同座標列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現只按土方安排忽略管線支承，既有設施因卸載或位移受損，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","textEn":"Apply the following check at handover: Compare detected utilities, road stages and excavation limits in shared coordinates. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If a spoil-only plan misses utility support and damages services through unloading or movement, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「開挖尺度與地表影響」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Excavation scale and surface impact\"?","options":["比對探測管線、道路分期及開挖邊界的共同座標。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","平均沉陷很小就代表鄰房一定沒有損傷"],"optionsEn":["Compare detected utilities, road stages and excavation limits in shared coordinates.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Small average settlement guarantees no damage to neighbouring buildings"],"answer":0,"explanation":"比對探測管線、道路分期及開挖邊界的共同座標。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare detected utilities, road stages and excavation limits in shared coordinates. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b166-v14-04","title":"開挖尺度與地表影響：失效診斷","titleEn":"Excavation scale and surface impact: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"],"prerequisiteIds":["b166-v14-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「開挖尺度與地表影響」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Excavation scale and surface impact” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只按土方安排忽略管線支承，既有設施因卸載或位移受損。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到比對探測管線、道路分期及開挖邊界的共同座標，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A spoil-only plan misses utility support and damages services through unloading or movement. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to compare detected utilities, road stages and excavation limits in shared coordinates to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：判別這個機制時，應觀察比對探測管線、道路分期及開挖邊界的共同座標；若出現只按土方安排忽略管線支承，既有設施因卸載或位移受損，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: If a spoil-only plan misses utility support and damages services through unloading or movement, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「土方體積相同就代表兩個明挖工程風險相同」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Equal excavation volume means identical risk for two cut-and-cover projects\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b166-v14-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只按土方安排忽略管線支承，既有設施因卸載或位移受損。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到比對探測管線、道路分期及開挖邊界的共同座標，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。","textEn":"A spoil-only plan misses utility support and damages services through unloading or movement. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to compare detected utilities, road stages and excavation limits in shared coordinates to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]},{"id":"b166-v14-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「開挖尺度與地表影響」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Excavation scale and surface impact\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","只按土方安排忽略管線支承，既有設施因卸載或位移受損。","所有擋土牆都可以直接使用完全主動土壓"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","A spoil-only plan misses utility support and damages services through unloading or movement.","Every retaining wall can directly use fully active earth pressure"],"answer":1,"explanation":"只按土方安排忽略管線支承，既有設施因卸載或位移受損。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A spoil-only plan misses utility support and damages services through unloading or movement. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b166-v14-05","title":"側向土壓與變形條件：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Lateral soil pressure and movement conditions: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"],"prerequisiteIds":["b166-v14-04"],"objective":"說明「側向土壓與變形條件」如何影響明挖覆蓋隧道施工的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Lateral soil pressure and movement conditions” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Cut-and-cover tunnel construction”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"主動土壓需要足夠牆體位移才可動員，鄰房敏感區的剛性支撐未必允許達到這個狀態。地表超載與水壓應分開處理，不能將總壓力都乘同一係數；簡化三角分布只用來理解量級，支撐牆需考慮分階段受力。 判別這個機制時，應觀察將牆體測斜與土層、超載及水位狀態共同比對；若出現用主動壓力描述幾乎不動的牆，低估支撐反力，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「側向土壓與變形條件」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Active pressure requires sufficient wall movement, which stiff restraint near sensitive buildings may prevent. Treat surcharge and water separately rather than multiplying total pressure by one coefficient. A triangular diagram gives scale, while a supported wall needs staged force redistribution and movement compatibility. Use the following check to discriminate the mechanism: Compare wall inclinometers with strata, surcharge and groundwater conditions. If active pressure applied to a nearly restrained wall understates brace reactions, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Lateral soil pressure and movement conditions” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：resultant=0.5*Ka*gamma*H^2=0.5*0.33*18 kN/m3*(8 m)^2=190.1 kN/m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: resultant=0.5*Ka*gamma*H^2=0.5*0.33*18 kN/m3*(8 m)^2=190.1 kN/m.","failure":"常見誤解：「所有擋土牆都可以直接使用完全主動土壓」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Every retaining wall can directly use fully active earth pressure\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「側向土壓與變形條件」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Lateral soil pressure and movement conditions”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b166-v14-05-k1","title":"側向土壓與變形條件","titleEn":"Lateral soil pressure and movement conditions","text":"主動土壓需要足夠牆體位移才可動員，鄰房敏感區的剛性支撐未必允許達到這個狀態。地表超載與水壓應分開處理，不能將總壓力都乘同一係數；簡化三角分布只用來理解量級，支撐牆需考慮分階段受力。","textEn":"Active pressure requires sufficient wall movement, which stiff restraint near sensitive buildings may prevent. Treat surcharge and water separately rather than multiplying total pressure by one coefficient.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]},{"id":"b166-v14-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：所有擋土牆都可以直接使用完全主動土壓 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Every retaining wall can directly use fully active earth pressure Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「側向土壓與變形條件」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Lateral soil pressure and movement conditions\" is correct?","options":["所有擋土牆都可以直接使用完全主動土壓","支撐荷重變大就只能是土壓增加","主動土壓需要足夠牆體位移才可動員，鄰房敏感區的剛性支撐未必允許達到這個狀態。"],"optionsEn":["Every retaining wall can directly use fully active earth pressure","Increasing brace force can only mean increasing earth pressure","Active pressure requires sufficient wall movement, which stiff restraint near sensitive buildings may prevent."],"answer":2,"explanation":"主動土壓需要足夠牆體位移才可動員，鄰房敏感區的剛性支撐未必允許達到這個狀態。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Active pressure requires sufficient wall movement, which stiff restraint near sensitive buildings may prevent. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b166-v14-06","title":"側向土壓與變形條件：定量估算","titleEn":"Lateral soil pressure and movement conditions: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"],"prerequisiteIds":["b166-v14-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「側向土壓與變形條件」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Lateral soil pressure and movement conditions” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：resultant=0.5*Ka*gamma*H^2=0.5*0.33*18 kN/m3*(8 m)^2=190.1 kN/m。開挖、結構施工與回填具有不同荷載路徑，竣工模型不能取代施工模型。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: resultant=0.5*Ka*gamma*H^2=0.5*0.33*18 kN/m3*(8 m)^2=190.1 kN/m. Excavation, structural work and backfilling have different load paths; the final model does not replace staged models. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將牆體測斜與土層、超載及水位狀態共同比對。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare wall inclinometers with strata, surcharge and groundwater conditions.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b166-v14-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：resultant=0.5*Ka*gamma*H^2=0.5*0.33*18 kN/m3*(8 m)^2=190.1 kN/m。開挖、結構施工與回填具有不同荷載路徑，竣工模型不能取代施工模型。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: resultant=0.5*Ka*gamma*H^2=0.5*0.33*18 kN/m3*(8 m)^2=190.1 kN/m. Excavation, structural work and backfilling have different load paths; the final model does not replace staged models. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]},{"id":"b166-v14-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「側向土壓與變形條件」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Lateral soil pressure and movement conditions\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：resultant=0.5*Ka*gamma*H^2=0.5*0.33*18 kN/m3*(8 m)^2=190.1 kN/m。","竣工抗浮合格就能保證每個施工階段都抗浮","永久樓板澆置完成就能立即取代全部臨時支撐"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: resultant=0.5*Ka*gamma*H^2=0.5*0.33*18 kN/m3*(8 m)^2=190.1 kN/m.","Passing permanent flotation checks guarantees every construction stage resists uplift","A freshly cast permanent slab immediately replaces every temporary brace"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：resultant=0.5*Ka*gamma*H^2=0.5*0.33*18 kN/m3*(8 m)^2=190.1 kN/m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: resultant=0.5*Ka*gamma*H^2=0.5*0.33*18 kN/m3*(8 m)^2=190.1 kN/m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b166-v14-07","title":"側向土壓與變形條件：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Lateral soil pressure and movement conditions: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"],"prerequisiteIds":["b166-v14-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「側向土壓與變形條件」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Lateral soil pressure and movement conditions” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將牆體測斜與土層、超載及水位狀態共同比對。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「用主動壓力描述幾乎不動的牆，低估支撐反力」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare wall inclinometers with strata, surcharge and groundwater conditions. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: Active pressure applied to a nearly restrained wall understates brace reactions. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將將牆體測斜與土層、超載及水位狀態共同比對列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現用主動壓力描述幾乎不動的牆，低估支撐反力，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","observationEn":"Site practice: Apply the following check at handover: Compare wall inclinometers with strata, surcharge and groundwater conditions. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If active pressure applied to a nearly restrained wall understates brace reactions, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","failure":"注意干擾：用主動壓力描述幾乎不動的牆，低估支撐反力。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Active pressure applied to a nearly restrained wall understates brace reactions. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b166-v14-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將牆體測斜與土層、超載及水位狀態共同比對。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「用主動壓力描述幾乎不動的牆，低估支撐反力」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。","textEn":"Compare wall inclinometers with strata, surcharge and groundwater conditions. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: Active pressure applied to a nearly restrained wall understates brace reactions. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]},{"id":"b166-v14-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將將牆體測斜與土層、超載及水位狀態共同比對列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現用主動壓力描述幾乎不動的牆，低估支撐反力，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","textEn":"Apply the following check at handover: Compare wall inclinometers with strata, surcharge and groundwater conditions. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If active pressure applied to a nearly restrained wall understates brace reactions, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「側向土壓與變形條件」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Lateral soil pressure and movement conditions\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","將牆體測斜與土層、超載及水位狀態共同比對。","回填越快完成就能保證施工階段更安全"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Compare wall inclinometers with strata, surcharge and groundwater conditions.","Faster completion of backfilling guarantees safer construction stages"],"answer":1,"explanation":"將牆體測斜與土層、超載及水位狀態共同比對。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare wall inclinometers with strata, surcharge and groundwater conditions. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b166-v14-08","title":"側向土壓與變形條件：失效診斷","titleEn":"Lateral soil pressure and movement conditions: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"],"prerequisiteIds":["b166-v14-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「側向土壓與變形條件」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Lateral soil pressure and movement conditions” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"用主動壓力描述幾乎不動的牆，低估支撐反力。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到將牆體測斜與土層、超載及水位狀態共同比對，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Active pressure applied to a nearly restrained wall understates brace reactions. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to compare wall inclinometers with strata, surcharge and groundwater conditions to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：判別這個機制時，應觀察將牆體測斜與土層、超載及水位狀態共同比對；若出現用主動壓力描述幾乎不動的牆，低估支撐反力，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: If active pressure applied to a nearly restrained wall understates brace reactions, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「所有擋土牆都可以直接使用完全主動土壓」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Every retaining wall can directly use fully active earth pressure\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b166-v14-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"用主動壓力描述幾乎不動的牆，低估支撐反力。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到將牆體測斜與土層、超載及水位狀態共同比對，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。","textEn":"Active pressure applied to a nearly restrained wall understates brace reactions. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to compare wall inclinometers with strata, surcharge and groundwater conditions to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]},{"id":"b166-v14-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「側向土壓與變形條件」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Lateral soil pressure and movement conditions\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","支撐荷重變大就只能是土壓增加","用主動壓力描述幾乎不動的牆，低估支撐反力。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Increasing brace force can only mean increasing earth pressure","Active pressure applied to a nearly restrained wall understates brace reactions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"用主動壓力描述幾乎不動的牆，低估支撐反力。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Active pressure applied to a nearly restrained wall understates brace reactions. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b166-v14-s2","title":"機制、材料與定量設計","titleEn":"Mechanisms, materials and quantitative design","description":"本階段聚焦「支撐軸力與溫度」與「底部隆起與抗浮區分」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Brace force and temperature\" and \"Base heave and uplift distinction\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b166-v14-09","title":"支撐軸力與溫度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Brace force and temperature: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"],"prerequisiteIds":["b166-v14-08"],"objective":"說明「支撐軸力與溫度」如何影響明挖覆蓋隧道施工的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Brace force and temperature” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Cut-and-cover tunnel construction”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"鋼支撐除了承受地層作用，也會隨溫度伸縮，受到拘束時產生額外軸力。荷重增加可能是熱效應而非牆後土壓增加，零點時間因此重要；比較力值要同步看溫度、牆移和接頭滑移，避免用單支荷重計判斷地層。 判別這個機制時，應觀察同步量測支撐溫度、軸力及兩端牆體位移；若出現日照升溫造成力峰被誤判地層失穩，錯誤調整支撐，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「支撐軸力與溫度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Steel braces expand thermally and develop extra force when restrained. A force increase can reflect temperature rather than rising earth pressure, making zero time important. Compare force with temperature, wall movement and joint slip instead of diagnosing ground solely from one load cell. Use the following check to discriminate the mechanism: Measure brace temperature, axial force and both wall-end movements simultaneously. If solar heating creates a force peak mistaken for ground instability and prompts an incorrect brace change, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Brace force and temperature” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：fullRestraintForce=E*A*alpha*dT=200 GPa*0.01 m2*12e-6/K*10 K=240 kN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: fullRestraintForce=E*A*alpha*dT=200 GPa*0.01 m2*12e-6/K*10 K=240 kN.","failure":"常見誤解：「支撐荷重變大就只能是土壓增加」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Increasing brace force can only mean increasing earth pressure\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「支撐軸力與溫度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Brace force and temperature”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b166-v14-09-k1","title":"支撐軸力與溫度","titleEn":"Brace force and temperature","text":"鋼支撐除了承受地層作用，也會隨溫度伸縮，受到拘束時產生額外軸力。荷重增加可能是熱效應而非牆後土壓增加，零點時間因此重要；比較力值要同步看溫度、牆移和接頭滑移，避免用單支荷重計判斷地層。","textEn":"Steel braces expand thermally and develop extra force when restrained. A force increase can reflect temperature rather than rising earth pressure, making zero time important.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]},{"id":"b166-v14-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：支撐荷重變大就只能是土壓增加 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Increasing brace force can only mean increasing earth pressure Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「支撐軸力與溫度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Brace force and temperature\" is correct?","options":["鋼支撐除了承受地層作用，也會隨溫度伸縮，受到拘束時產生額外軸力。","支撐荷重變大就只能是土壓增加","基底往上動的所有原因都屬同一種失效"],"optionsEn":["Steel braces expand thermally and develop extra force when restrained.","Increasing brace force can only mean increasing earth pressure","Every cause of upward base movement is the same failure mechanism"],"answer":0,"explanation":"鋼支撐除了承受地層作用，也會隨溫度伸縮，受到拘束時產生額外軸力。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Steel braces expand thermally and develop extra force when restrained. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b166-v14-10","title":"支撐軸力與溫度：定量估算","titleEn":"Brace force and temperature: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"],"prerequisiteIds":["b166-v14-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「支撐軸力與溫度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Brace force and temperature” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：fullRestraintForce=E*A*alpha*dT=200 GPa*0.01 m2*12e-6/K*10 K=240 kN。開挖、結構施工與回填具有不同荷載路徑，竣工模型不能取代施工模型。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: fullRestraintForce=E*A*alpha*dT=200 GPa*0.01 m2*12e-6/K*10 K=240 kN. Excavation, structural work and backfilling have different load paths; the final model does not replace staged models. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同步量測支撐溫度、軸力及兩端牆體位移。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure brace temperature, axial force and both wall-end movements simultaneously.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b166-v14-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：fullRestraintForce=E*A*alpha*dT=200 GPa*0.01 m2*12e-6/K*10 K=240 kN。開挖、結構施工與回填具有不同荷載路徑，竣工模型不能取代施工模型。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: fullRestraintForce=E*A*alpha*dT=200 GPa*0.01 m2*12e-6/K*10 K=240 kN. Excavation, structural work and backfilling have different load paths; the final model does not replace staged models. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]},{"id":"b166-v14-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「支撐軸力與溫度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Brace force and temperature\", which statement holds?","options":["箱體牆面不裂就能保證所有穿牆位置都不漏","原創教學假設：fullRestraintForce=E*A*alpha*dT=200 GPa*0.01 m2*12e-6/K*10 K=240 kN。","平均沉陷很小就代表鄰房一定沒有損傷"],"optionsEn":["Uncracked box walls guarantee every penetration remains watertight","Original teaching assumptions: fullRestraintForce=E*A*alpha*dT=200 GPa*0.01 m2*12e-6/K*10 K=240 kN.","Small average settlement guarantees no damage to neighbouring buildings"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：fullRestraintForce=E*A*alpha*dT=200 GPa*0.01 m2*12e-6/K*10 K=240 kN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: fullRestraintForce=E*A*alpha*dT=200 GPa*0.01 m2*12e-6/K*10 K=240 kN. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b166-v14-11","title":"支撐軸力與溫度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Brace force and temperature: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"],"prerequisiteIds":["b166-v14-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「支撐軸力與溫度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Brace force and temperature” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同步量測支撐溫度、軸力及兩端牆體位移。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「日照升溫造成力峰被誤判地層失穩，錯誤調整支撐」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure brace temperature, axial force and both wall-end movements simultaneously. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: Solar heating creates a force peak mistaken for ground instability and prompts an incorrect brace change. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將同步量測支撐溫度、軸力及兩端牆體位移列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現日照升溫造成力峰被誤判地層失穩，錯誤調整支撐，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","observationEn":"Site practice: Apply the following check at handover: Measure brace temperature, axial force and both wall-end movements simultaneously. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If solar heating creates a force peak mistaken for ground instability and prompts an incorrect brace change, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","failure":"注意干擾：日照升溫造成力峰被誤判地層失穩，錯誤調整支撐。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Solar heating creates a force peak mistaken for ground instability and prompts an incorrect brace change. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b166-v14-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同步量測支撐溫度、軸力及兩端牆體位移。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「日照升溫造成力峰被誤判地層失穩，錯誤調整支撐」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。","textEn":"Measure brace temperature, axial force and both wall-end movements simultaneously. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: Solar heating creates a force peak mistaken for ground instability and prompts an incorrect brace change. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]},{"id":"b166-v14-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將同步量測支撐溫度、軸力及兩端牆體位移列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現日照升溫造成力峰被誤判地層失穩，錯誤調整支撐，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","textEn":"Apply the following check at handover: Measure brace temperature, axial force and both wall-end movements simultaneously. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If solar heating creates a force peak mistaken for ground instability and prompts an incorrect brace change, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「支撐軸力與溫度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Brace force and temperature\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","道路恢復平整就表示全部地下工程已完成驗證","同步量測支撐溫度、軸力及兩端牆體位移。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","A smooth restored road proves all underground works have been verified","Measure brace temperature, axial force and both wall-end movements simultaneously."],"answer":2,"explanation":"同步量測支撐溫度、軸力及兩端牆體位移。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure brace temperature, axial force and both wall-end movements simultaneously. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b166-v14-12","title":"支撐軸力與溫度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Brace force and temperature: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"],"prerequisiteIds":["b166-v14-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「支撐軸力與溫度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Brace force and temperature” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"日照升溫造成力峰被誤判地層失穩，錯誤調整支撐。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到同步量測支撐溫度、軸力及兩端牆體位移，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Solar heating creates a force peak mistaken for ground instability and prompts an incorrect brace change. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to measure brace temperature, axial force and both wall-end movements simultaneously to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：判別這個機制時，應觀察同步量測支撐溫度、軸力及兩端牆體位移；若出現日照升溫造成力峰被誤判地層失穩，錯誤調整支撐，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: If solar heating creates a force peak mistaken for ground instability and prompts an incorrect brace change, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「支撐荷重變大就只能是土壓增加」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Increasing brace force can only mean increasing earth pressure\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b166-v14-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"日照升溫造成力峰被誤判地層失穩，錯誤調整支撐。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到同步量測支撐溫度、軸力及兩端牆體位移，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。","textEn":"Solar heating creates a force peak mistaken for ground instability and prompts an incorrect brace change. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to measure brace temperature, axial force and both wall-end movements simultaneously to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]},{"id":"b166-v14-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「支撐軸力與溫度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Brace force and temperature\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["日照升溫造成力峰被誤判地層失穩，錯誤調整支撐。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","基底往上動的所有原因都屬同一種失效"],"optionsEn":["Solar heating creates a force peak mistaken for ground instability and prompts an incorrect brace change.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Every cause of upward base movement is the same failure mechanism"],"answer":0,"explanation":"日照升溫造成力峰被誤判地層失穩，錯誤調整支撐。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Solar heating creates a force peak mistaken for ground instability and prompts an incorrect brace change. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b166-v14-13","title":"底部隆起與抗浮區分：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Base heave and uplift distinction: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"],"prerequisiteIds":["b166-v14-12"],"objective":"說明「底部隆起與抗浮區分」如何影響明挖覆蓋隧道施工的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Base heave and uplift distinction” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Cut-and-cover tunnel construction”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"軟黏土底部隆起與承壓水造成的水力抬升有不同機制，不能以同一重量比處理。開挖卸載降低上覆應力，地層剪切與水壓都可能變得重要；調查需把不排水強度、滲透層和測壓水位分開建模。 判別這個機制時，應觀察比較底部位移、分層孔壓及地層強度資料；若出現把水力抬升當普通沉陷調整標高，未處理真正水壓，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「底部隆起與抗浮區分」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Undrained clay heave and hydraulic uplift are different mechanisms and cannot share one simple weight ratio. Excavation removes overburden, increasing the importance of shear stability and pore pressure. Model undrained strength, permeable layers and piezometric level separately rather than merging all bottom movement. Use the following check to discriminate the mechanism: Compare base movement, interval pore pressures and ground-strength evidence. If hydraulic uplift is treated as ordinary settlement correction without addressing the pressure source, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Base heave and uplift distinction” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：waterUplift=gammaW*h*A=9.81 kN/m3*5 m*100 m2=4905 kN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: waterUplift=gammaW*h*A=9.81 kN/m3*5 m*100 m2=4905 kN.","failure":"常見誤解：「基底往上動的所有原因都屬同一種失效」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Every cause of upward base movement is the same failure mechanism\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「底部隆起與抗浮區分」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Base heave and uplift distinction”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b166-v14-13-k1","title":"底部隆起與抗浮區分","titleEn":"Base heave and uplift distinction","text":"軟黏土底部隆起與承壓水造成的水力抬升有不同機制，不能以同一重量比處理。開挖卸載降低上覆應力，地層剪切與水壓都可能變得重要；調查需把不排水強度、滲透層和測壓水位分開建模。","textEn":"Undrained clay heave and hydraulic uplift are different mechanisms and cannot share one simple weight ratio. Excavation removes overburden, increasing the importance of shear stability and pore pressure.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]},{"id":"b166-v14-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：基底往上動的所有原因都屬同一種失效 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Every cause of upward base movement is the same failure mechanism Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「底部隆起與抗浮區分」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Base heave and uplift distinction\" is correct?","options":["基底往上動的所有原因都屬同一種失效","軟黏土底部隆起與承壓水造成的水力抬升有不同機制，不能以同一重量比處理。","竣工抗浮合格就能保證每個施工階段都抗浮"],"optionsEn":["Every cause of upward base movement is the same failure mechanism","Undrained clay heave and hydraulic uplift are different mechanisms and cannot share one simple weight ratio.","Passing permanent flotation checks guarantees every construction stage resists uplift"],"answer":1,"explanation":"軟黏土底部隆起與承壓水造成的水力抬升有不同機制，不能以同一重量比處理。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Undrained clay heave and hydraulic uplift are different mechanisms and cannot share one simple weight ratio. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b166-v14-14","title":"底部隆起與抗浮區分：定量估算","titleEn":"Base heave and uplift distinction: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"],"prerequisiteIds":["b166-v14-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「底部隆起與抗浮區分」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Base heave and uplift distinction” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：waterUplift=gammaW*h*A=9.81 kN/m3*5 m*100 m2=4905 kN。開挖、結構施工與回填具有不同荷載路徑，竣工模型不能取代施工模型。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: waterUplift=gammaW*h*A=9.81 kN/m3*5 m*100 m2=4905 kN. Excavation, structural work and backfilling have different load paths; the final model does not replace staged models. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比較底部位移、分層孔壓及地層強度資料。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare base movement, interval pore pressures and ground-strength evidence.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b166-v14-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：waterUplift=gammaW*h*A=9.81 kN/m3*5 m*100 m2=4905 kN。開挖、結構施工與回填具有不同荷載路徑，竣工模型不能取代施工模型。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: waterUplift=gammaW*h*A=9.81 kN/m3*5 m*100 m2=4905 kN. Excavation, structural work and backfilling have different load paths; the final model does not replace staged models. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]},{"id":"b166-v14-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「底部隆起與抗浮區分」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Base heave and uplift distinction\", which statement holds?","options":["永久樓板澆置完成就能立即取代全部臨時支撐","回填越快完成就能保證施工階段更安全","原創教學假設：waterUplift=gammaW*h*A=9.81 kN/m3*5 m*100 m2=4905 kN。"],"optionsEn":["A freshly cast permanent slab immediately replaces every temporary brace","Faster completion of backfilling guarantees safer construction stages","Original teaching assumptions: waterUplift=gammaW*h*A=9.81 kN/m3*5 m*100 m2=4905 kN."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：waterUplift=gammaW*h*A=9.81 kN/m3*5 m*100 m2=4905 kN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: waterUplift=gammaW*h*A=9.81 kN/m3*5 m*100 m2=4905 kN. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b166-v14-15","title":"底部隆起與抗浮區分：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Base heave and uplift distinction: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"],"prerequisiteIds":["b166-v14-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「底部隆起與抗浮區分」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Base heave and uplift distinction” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比較底部位移、分層孔壓及地層強度資料。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「把水力抬升當普通沉陷調整標高，未處理真正水壓」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare base movement, interval pore pressures and ground-strength evidence. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: Hydraulic uplift is treated as ordinary settlement correction without addressing the pressure source. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將比較底部位移、分層孔壓及地層強度資料列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現把水力抬升當普通沉陷調整標高，未處理真正水壓，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","observationEn":"Site practice: Apply the following check at handover: Compare base movement, interval pore pressures and ground-strength evidence. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If hydraulic uplift is treated as ordinary settlement correction without addressing the pressure source, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","failure":"注意干擾：把水力抬升當普通沉陷調整標高，未處理真正水壓。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Hydraulic uplift is treated as ordinary settlement correction without addressing the pressure source. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b166-v14-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比較底部位移、分層孔壓及地層強度資料。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「把水力抬升當普通沉陷調整標高，未處理真正水壓」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。","textEn":"Compare base movement, interval pore pressures and ground-strength evidence. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: Hydraulic uplift is treated as ordinary settlement correction without addressing the pressure source. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]},{"id":"b166-v14-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將比較底部位移、分層孔壓及地層強度資料列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現把水力抬升當普通沉陷調整標高，未處理真正水壓，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","textEn":"Apply the following check at handover: Compare base movement, interval pore pressures and ground-strength evidence. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If hydraulic uplift is treated as ordinary settlement correction without addressing the pressure source, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「底部隆起與抗浮區分」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Base heave and uplift distinction\"?","options":["比較底部位移、分層孔壓及地層強度資料。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","土方體積相同就代表兩個明挖工程風險相同"],"optionsEn":["Compare base movement, interval pore pressures and ground-strength evidence.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Equal excavation volume means identical risk for two cut-and-cover projects"],"answer":0,"explanation":"比較底部位移、分層孔壓及地層強度資料。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare base movement, interval pore pressures and ground-strength evidence. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b166-v14-16","title":"底部隆起與抗浮區分：失效診斷","titleEn":"Base heave and uplift distinction: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"],"prerequisiteIds":["b166-v14-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「底部隆起與抗浮區分」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Base heave and uplift distinction” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把水力抬升當普通沉陷調整標高，未處理真正水壓。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到比較底部位移、分層孔壓及地層強度資料，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Hydraulic uplift is treated as ordinary settlement correction without addressing the pressure source. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to compare base movement, interval pore pressures and ground-strength evidence to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：判別這個機制時，應觀察比較底部位移、分層孔壓及地層強度資料；若出現把水力抬升當普通沉陷調整標高，未處理真正水壓，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: If hydraulic uplift is treated as ordinary settlement correction without addressing the pressure source, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「基底往上動的所有原因都屬同一種失效」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Every cause of upward base movement is the same failure mechanism\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b166-v14-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把水力抬升當普通沉陷調整標高，未處理真正水壓。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到比較底部位移、分層孔壓及地層強度資料，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。","textEn":"Hydraulic uplift is treated as ordinary settlement correction without addressing the pressure source. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to compare base movement, interval pore pressures and ground-strength evidence to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]},{"id":"b166-v14-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「底部隆起與抗浮區分」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Base heave and uplift distinction\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","把水力抬升當普通沉陷調整標高，未處理真正水壓。","竣工抗浮合格就能保證每個施工階段都抗浮"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Hydraulic uplift is treated as ordinary settlement correction without addressing the pressure source.","Passing permanent flotation checks guarantees every construction stage resists uplift"],"answer":1,"explanation":"把水力抬升當普通沉陷調整標高，未處理真正水壓。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Hydraulic uplift is treated as ordinary settlement correction without addressing the pressure source. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b166-v14-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「箱體自重與施工抗浮」與「防水接縫與穿牆構件」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Box weight and temporary flotation\" and \"Waterproof joints and penetrations\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b166-v14-17","title":"箱體自重與施工抗浮：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Box weight and temporary flotation: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"],"prerequisiteIds":["b166-v14-16"],"objective":"說明「箱體自重與施工抗浮」如何影響明挖覆蓋隧道施工的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Box weight and temporary flotation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Cut-and-cover tunnel construction”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"永久覆土可提供重量，但施工中尚未回填時並不存在這份抗浮作用。空箱體、局部回填與封頂後各有不同邊界，水位也可能回升；重量帳必須只計入當階段確實存在且可傳力的部分，不得提前借用竣工狀態。 判別這個機制時，應觀察逐階段核對實際重量、回填範圍與可達水位；若出現尚未回填便使用永久覆土重量，空箱體出現抬升，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「箱體自重與施工抗浮」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Permanent cover supplies weight but is absent before backfilling. Empty boxes, partial fill and completed roofs have different boundaries and may encounter rising groundwater. Count only weight physically present and connected in each stage rather than borrowing resistance from the completed structure. Use the following check to discriminate the mechanism: Audit actual weight, backfill extent and possible water levels at every stage. If using future cover weight allows an unbackfilled box to lift, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Box weight and temporary flotation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：weightToUplift=presentWeight/uplift=6000 kN/4905 kN=1.223, not a code factor。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: weightToUplift=presentWeight/uplift=6000 kN/4905 kN=1.223, not a code factor.","failure":"常見誤解：「竣工抗浮合格就能保證每個施工階段都抗浮」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Passing permanent flotation checks guarantees every construction stage resists uplift\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「箱體自重與施工抗浮」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Box weight and temporary flotation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b166-v14-17-k1","title":"箱體自重與施工抗浮","titleEn":"Box weight and temporary flotation","text":"永久覆土可提供重量，但施工中尚未回填時並不存在這份抗浮作用。空箱體、局部回填與封頂後各有不同邊界，水位也可能回升；重量帳必須只計入當階段確實存在且可傳力的部分，不得提前借用竣工狀態。","textEn":"Permanent cover supplies weight but is absent before backfilling. Empty boxes, partial fill and completed roofs have different boundaries and may encounter rising groundwater.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]},{"id":"b166-v14-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：竣工抗浮合格就能保證每個施工階段都抗浮 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Passing permanent flotation checks guarantees every construction stage resists uplift Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「箱體自重與施工抗浮」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Box weight and temporary flotation\" is correct?","options":["竣工抗浮合格就能保證每個施工階段都抗浮","箱體牆面不裂就能保證所有穿牆位置都不漏","永久覆土可提供重量，但施工中尚未回填時並不存在這份抗浮作用。"],"optionsEn":["Passing permanent flotation checks guarantees every construction stage resists uplift","Uncracked box walls guarantee every penetration remains watertight","Permanent cover supplies weight but is absent before backfilling."],"answer":2,"explanation":"永久覆土可提供重量，但施工中尚未回填時並不存在這份抗浮作用。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Permanent cover supplies weight but is absent before backfilling. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b166-v14-18","title":"箱體自重與施工抗浮：定量估算","titleEn":"Box weight and temporary flotation: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"],"prerequisiteIds":["b166-v14-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「箱體自重與施工抗浮」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Box weight and temporary flotation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：weightToUplift=presentWeight/uplift=6000 kN/4905 kN=1.223, not a code factor。開挖、結構施工與回填具有不同荷載路徑，竣工模型不能取代施工模型。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: weightToUplift=presentWeight/uplift=6000 kN/4905 kN=1.223, not a code factor. Excavation, structural work and backfilling have different load paths; the final model does not replace staged models. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：逐階段核對實際重量、回填範圍與可達水位。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Audit actual weight, backfill extent and possible water levels at every stage.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b166-v14-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：weightToUplift=presentWeight/uplift=6000 kN/4905 kN=1.223, not a code factor。開挖、結構施工與回填具有不同荷載路徑，竣工模型不能取代施工模型。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: weightToUplift=presentWeight/uplift=6000 kN/4905 kN=1.223, not a code factor. Excavation, structural work and backfilling have different load paths; the final model does not replace staged models. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]},{"id":"b166-v14-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「箱體自重與施工抗浮」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Box weight and temporary flotation\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：weightToUplift=presentWeight/uplift=6000 kN/4905 kN=1.223, not a code factor。","平均沉陷很小就代表鄰房一定沒有損傷","道路恢復平整就表示全部地下工程已完成驗證"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: weightToUplift=presentWeight/uplift=6000 kN/4905 kN=1.223, not a code factor.","Small average settlement guarantees no damage to neighbouring buildings","A smooth restored road proves all underground works have been verified"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：weightToUplift=presentWeight/uplift=6000 kN/4905 kN=1.223, not a code factor。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: weightToUplift=presentWeight/uplift=6000 kN/4905 kN=1.223, not a code factor. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b166-v14-19","title":"箱體自重與施工抗浮：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Box weight and temporary flotation: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"],"prerequisiteIds":["b166-v14-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「箱體自重與施工抗浮」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Box weight and temporary flotation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"逐階段核對實際重量、回填範圍與可達水位。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「尚未回填便使用永久覆土重量，空箱體出現抬升」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Audit actual weight, backfill extent and possible water levels at every stage. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: Using future cover weight allows an unbackfilled box to lift. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將逐階段核對實際重量、回填範圍與可達水位列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現尚未回填便使用永久覆土重量，空箱體出現抬升，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","observationEn":"Site practice: Apply the following check at handover: Audit actual weight, backfill extent and possible water levels at every stage. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If using future cover weight allows an unbackfilled box to lift, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","failure":"注意干擾：尚未回填便使用永久覆土重量，空箱體出現抬升。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using future cover weight allows an unbackfilled box to lift. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b166-v14-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"逐階段核對實際重量、回填範圍與可達水位。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「尚未回填便使用永久覆土重量，空箱體出現抬升」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。","textEn":"Audit actual weight, backfill extent and possible water levels at every stage. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: Using future cover weight allows an unbackfilled box to lift. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]},{"id":"b166-v14-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將逐階段核對實際重量、回填範圍與可達水位列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現尚未回填便使用永久覆土重量，空箱體出現抬升，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","textEn":"Apply the following check at handover: Audit actual weight, backfill extent and possible water levels at every stage. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If using future cover weight allows an unbackfilled box to lift, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「箱體自重與施工抗浮」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Box weight and temporary flotation\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","逐階段核對實際重量、回填範圍與可達水位。","所有擋土牆都可以直接使用完全主動土壓"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Audit actual weight, backfill extent and possible water levels at every stage.","Every retaining wall can directly use fully active earth pressure"],"answer":1,"explanation":"逐階段核對實際重量、回填範圍與可達水位。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Audit actual weight, backfill extent and possible water levels at every stage. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b166-v14-20","title":"箱體自重與施工抗浮：失效診斷","titleEn":"Box weight and temporary flotation: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"],"prerequisiteIds":["b166-v14-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「箱體自重與施工抗浮」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Box weight and temporary flotation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"尚未回填便使用永久覆土重量，空箱體出現抬升。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到逐階段核對實際重量、回填範圍與可達水位，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using future cover weight allows an unbackfilled box to lift. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to audit actual weight, backfill extent and possible water levels at every stage to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：判別這個機制時，應觀察逐階段核對實際重量、回填範圍與可達水位；若出現尚未回填便使用永久覆土重量，空箱體出現抬升，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: If using future cover weight allows an unbackfilled box to lift, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「竣工抗浮合格就能保證每個施工階段都抗浮」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Passing permanent flotation checks guarantees every construction stage resists uplift\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b166-v14-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"尚未回填便使用永久覆土重量，空箱體出現抬升。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到逐階段核對實際重量、回填範圍與可達水位，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。","textEn":"Using future cover weight allows an unbackfilled box to lift. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to audit actual weight, backfill extent and possible water levels at every stage to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]},{"id":"b166-v14-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「箱體自重與施工抗浮」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Box weight and temporary flotation\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","箱體牆面不裂就能保證所有穿牆位置都不漏","尚未回填便使用永久覆土重量，空箱體出現抬升。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Uncracked box walls guarantee every penetration remains watertight","Using future cover weight allows an unbackfilled box to lift."],"answer":2,"explanation":"尚未回填便使用永久覆土重量，空箱體出現抬升。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using future cover weight allows an unbackfilled box to lift. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b166-v14-21","title":"防水接縫與穿牆構件：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Waterproof joints and penetrations: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"],"prerequisiteIds":["b166-v14-20"],"objective":"說明「防水接縫與穿牆構件」如何影響明挖覆蓋隧道施工的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Waterproof joints and penetrations” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Cut-and-cover tunnel construction”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"明挖箱體常有施工縫、伸縮縫及大量管線穿牆，止水連續性由這些界面控制。接縫位移與水壓可能同時存在，單獨材料試驗不能證明安裝系統；驗證需把預埋位置、固定狀態及兩側結構變形連在一起。 判別這個機制時，應觀察核對止水帶連續、穿牆套管及接縫變形紀錄；若出現穿牆套管與止水細部不連續，漏水沿界面繞過膜材，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「防水接縫與穿牆構件」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Cut-and-cover boxes contain construction joints, movement joints and penetrations that govern waterproof continuity. Movement and pressure can coexist, so isolated material tests do not prove installation. Link embedded position, restraint and deformation of adjacent structure rather than checking the seal alone. Use the following check to discriminate the mechanism: Audit waterstop continuity, wall sleeves and joint-movement records. If a discontinuous sleeve detail lets water bypass the membrane along an interface, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Waterproof joints and penetrations” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：jointStrain=movement/freeSealLength=4 mm/80 mm=0.05。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: jointStrain=movement/freeSealLength=4 mm/80 mm=0.05.","failure":"常見誤解：「箱體牆面不裂就能保證所有穿牆位置都不漏」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Uncracked box walls guarantee every penetration remains watertight\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「防水接縫與穿牆構件」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Waterproof joints and penetrations”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b166-v14-21-k1","title":"防水接縫與穿牆構件","titleEn":"Waterproof joints and penetrations","text":"明挖箱體常有施工縫、伸縮縫及大量管線穿牆，止水連續性由這些界面控制。接縫位移與水壓可能同時存在，單獨材料試驗不能證明安裝系統；驗證需把預埋位置、固定狀態及兩側結構變形連在一起。","textEn":"Cut-and-cover boxes contain construction joints, movement joints and penetrations that govern waterproof continuity. Movement and pressure can coexist, so isolated material tests do not prove installation.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]},{"id":"b166-v14-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：箱體牆面不裂就能保證所有穿牆位置都不漏 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Uncracked box walls guarantee every penetration remains watertight Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「防水接縫與穿牆構件」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Waterproof joints and penetrations\" is correct?","options":["明挖箱體常有施工縫、伸縮縫及大量管線穿牆，止水連續性由這些界面控制。","箱體牆面不裂就能保證所有穿牆位置都不漏","永久樓板澆置完成就能立即取代全部臨時支撐"],"optionsEn":["Cut-and-cover boxes contain construction joints, movement joints and penetrations that govern waterproof continuity.","Uncracked box walls guarantee every penetration remains watertight","A freshly cast permanent slab immediately replaces every temporary brace"],"answer":0,"explanation":"明挖箱體常有施工縫、伸縮縫及大量管線穿牆，止水連續性由這些界面控制。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Cut-and-cover boxes contain construction joints, movement joints and penetrations that govern waterproof continuity. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b166-v14-22","title":"防水接縫與穿牆構件：定量估算","titleEn":"Waterproof joints and penetrations: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"],"prerequisiteIds":["b166-v14-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「防水接縫與穿牆構件」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Waterproof joints and penetrations” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：jointStrain=movement/freeSealLength=4 mm/80 mm=0.05。開挖、結構施工與回填具有不同荷載路徑，竣工模型不能取代施工模型。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: jointStrain=movement/freeSealLength=4 mm/80 mm=0.05. Excavation, structural work and backfilling have different load paths; the final model does not replace staged models. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對止水帶連續、穿牆套管及接縫變形紀錄。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Audit waterstop continuity, wall sleeves and joint-movement records.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b166-v14-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：jointStrain=movement/freeSealLength=4 mm/80 mm=0.05。開挖、結構施工與回填具有不同荷載路徑，竣工模型不能取代施工模型。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: jointStrain=movement/freeSealLength=4 mm/80 mm=0.05. Excavation, structural work and backfilling have different load paths; the final model does not replace staged models. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]},{"id":"b166-v14-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「防水接縫與穿牆構件」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Waterproof joints and penetrations\", which statement holds?","options":["回填越快完成就能保證施工階段更安全","原創教學假設：jointStrain=movement/freeSealLength=4 mm/80 mm=0.05。","土方體積相同就代表兩個明挖工程風險相同"],"optionsEn":["Faster completion of backfilling guarantees safer construction stages","Original teaching assumptions: jointStrain=movement/freeSealLength=4 mm/80 mm=0.05.","Equal excavation volume means identical risk for two cut-and-cover projects"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：jointStrain=movement/freeSealLength=4 mm/80 mm=0.05。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: jointStrain=movement/freeSealLength=4 mm/80 mm=0.05. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b166-v14-23","title":"防水接縫與穿牆構件：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Waterproof joints and penetrations: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"],"prerequisiteIds":["b166-v14-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「防水接縫與穿牆構件」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Waterproof joints and penetrations” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對止水帶連續、穿牆套管及接縫變形紀錄。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「穿牆套管與止水細部不連續，漏水沿界面繞過膜材」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Audit waterstop continuity, wall sleeves and joint-movement records. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: A discontinuous sleeve detail lets water bypass the membrane along an interface. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將核對止水帶連續、穿牆套管及接縫變形紀錄列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現穿牆套管與止水細部不連續，漏水沿界面繞過膜材，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","observationEn":"Site practice: Apply the following check at handover: Audit waterstop continuity, wall sleeves and joint-movement records. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If a discontinuous sleeve detail lets water bypass the membrane along an interface, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","failure":"注意干擾：穿牆套管與止水細部不連續，漏水沿界面繞過膜材。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A discontinuous sleeve detail lets water bypass the membrane along an interface. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b166-v14-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對止水帶連續、穿牆套管及接縫變形紀錄。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「穿牆套管與止水細部不連續，漏水沿界面繞過膜材」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。","textEn":"Audit waterstop continuity, wall sleeves and joint-movement records. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: A discontinuous sleeve detail lets water bypass the membrane along an interface. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]},{"id":"b166-v14-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將核對止水帶連續、穿牆套管及接縫變形紀錄列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現穿牆套管與止水細部不連續，漏水沿界面繞過膜材，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","textEn":"Apply the following check at handover: Audit waterstop continuity, wall sleeves and joint-movement records. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If a discontinuous sleeve detail lets water bypass the membrane along an interface, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「防水接縫與穿牆構件」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Waterproof joints and penetrations\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","支撐荷重變大就只能是土壓增加","核對止水帶連續、穿牆套管及接縫變形紀錄。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Increasing brace force can only mean increasing earth pressure","Audit waterstop continuity, wall sleeves and joint-movement records."],"answer":2,"explanation":"核對止水帶連續、穿牆套管及接縫變形紀錄。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Audit waterstop continuity, wall sleeves and joint-movement records. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b166-v14-24","title":"防水接縫與穿牆構件：失效診斷","titleEn":"Waterproof joints and penetrations: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"],"prerequisiteIds":["b166-v14-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「防水接縫與穿牆構件」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Waterproof joints and penetrations” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"穿牆套管與止水細部不連續，漏水沿界面繞過膜材。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到核對止水帶連續、穿牆套管及接縫變形紀錄，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A discontinuous sleeve detail lets water bypass the membrane along an interface. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to audit waterstop continuity, wall sleeves and joint-movement records to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：判別這個機制時，應觀察核對止水帶連續、穿牆套管及接縫變形紀錄；若出現穿牆套管與止水細部不連續，漏水沿界面繞過膜材，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: If a discontinuous sleeve detail lets water bypass the membrane along an interface, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「箱體牆面不裂就能保證所有穿牆位置都不漏」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Uncracked box walls guarantee every penetration remains watertight\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b166-v14-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"穿牆套管與止水細部不連續，漏水沿界面繞過膜材。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到核對止水帶連續、穿牆套管及接縫變形紀錄，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。","textEn":"A discontinuous sleeve detail lets water bypass the membrane along an interface. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to audit waterstop continuity, wall sleeves and joint-movement records to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]},{"id":"b166-v14-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「防水接縫與穿牆構件」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Waterproof joints and penetrations\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["穿牆套管與止水細部不連續，漏水沿界面繞過膜材。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","永久樓板澆置完成就能立即取代全部臨時支撐"],"optionsEn":["A discontinuous sleeve detail lets water bypass the membrane along an interface.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","A freshly cast permanent slab immediately replaces every temporary brace"],"answer":0,"explanation":"穿牆套管與止水細部不連續，漏水沿界面繞過膜材。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A discontinuous sleeve detail lets water bypass the membrane along an interface. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b166-v14-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「支撐拆換與荷載轉移」與「鄰房沉陷與角變形」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Brace removal and load transfer\" and \"Neighbour settlement and angular distortion\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b166-v14-25","title":"支撐拆換與荷載轉移：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Brace removal and load transfer: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"],"prerequisiteIds":["b166-v14-24"],"objective":"說明「支撐拆換與荷載轉移」如何影響明挖覆蓋隧道施工的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Brace removal and load transfer” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Cut-and-cover tunnel construction”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"臨時支撐拆除將側向荷載轉到永久樓板和牆，混凝土齡期與接頭完成度決定能否接手。竣工樓板存在不代表當天已具備預期剛度，開口也會切斷壓力路徑；拆換模型需按實際順序逐階段檢核。 判別這個機制時，應觀察對照樓板成熟證據、接頭完成及拆換前後應變；若出現接頭尚未傳力就拆支撐，牆移突增並使樓板邊緣開裂，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「支撐拆換與荷載轉移」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Removing temporary braces transfers lateral actions to slabs and walls whose age and joint completion govern engagement. A slab's presence does not prove its intended stiffness, and openings interrupt compression paths. Assess removal in the actual sequence rather than using only the final configuration. Use the following check to discriminate the mechanism: Compare slab maturity, joint completion and strains before and after load transfer. If removing a brace before joint engagement increases wall movement and cracks slab edges, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Brace removal and load transfer” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：transferredReaction=removedBraceForce/engagedSlabWidth=900 kN/6 m=150 kN/m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: transferredReaction=removedBraceForce/engagedSlabWidth=900 kN/6 m=150 kN/m.","failure":"常見誤解：「永久樓板澆置完成就能立即取代全部臨時支撐」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A freshly cast permanent slab immediately replaces every temporary brace\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「支撐拆換與荷載轉移」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Brace removal and load transfer”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b166-v14-25-k1","title":"支撐拆換與荷載轉移","titleEn":"Brace removal and load transfer","text":"臨時支撐拆除將側向荷載轉到永久樓板和牆，混凝土齡期與接頭完成度決定能否接手。竣工樓板存在不代表當天已具備預期剛度，開口也會切斷壓力路徑；拆換模型需按實際順序逐階段檢核。","textEn":"Removing temporary braces transfers lateral actions to slabs and walls whose age and joint completion govern engagement. A slab's presence does not prove its intended stiffness, and openings interrupt compression paths.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]},{"id":"b166-v14-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：永久樓板澆置完成就能立即取代全部臨時支撐 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A freshly cast permanent slab immediately replaces every temporary brace Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「支撐拆換與荷載轉移」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Brace removal and load transfer\" is correct?","options":["永久樓板澆置完成就能立即取代全部臨時支撐","臨時支撐拆除將側向荷載轉到永久樓板和牆，混凝土齡期與接頭完成度決定能否接手。","平均沉陷很小就代表鄰房一定沒有損傷"],"optionsEn":["A freshly cast permanent slab immediately replaces every temporary brace","Removing temporary braces transfers lateral actions to slabs and walls whose age and joint completion govern engagement.","Small average settlement guarantees no damage to neighbouring buildings"],"answer":1,"explanation":"臨時支撐拆除將側向荷載轉到永久樓板和牆，混凝土齡期與接頭完成度決定能否接手。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Removing temporary braces transfers lateral actions to slabs and walls whose age and joint completion govern engagement. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b166-v14-26","title":"支撐拆換與荷載轉移：定量估算","titleEn":"Brace removal and load transfer: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"],"prerequisiteIds":["b166-v14-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「支撐拆換與荷載轉移」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Brace removal and load transfer” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：transferredReaction=removedBraceForce/engagedSlabWidth=900 kN/6 m=150 kN/m。開挖、結構施工與回填具有不同荷載路徑，竣工模型不能取代施工模型。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: transferredReaction=removedBraceForce/engagedSlabWidth=900 kN/6 m=150 kN/m. Excavation, structural work and backfilling have different load paths; the final model does not replace staged models. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：對照樓板成熟證據、接頭完成及拆換前後應變。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare slab maturity, joint completion and strains before and after load transfer.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b166-v14-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：transferredReaction=removedBraceForce/engagedSlabWidth=900 kN/6 m=150 kN/m。開挖、結構施工與回填具有不同荷載路徑，竣工模型不能取代施工模型。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: transferredReaction=removedBraceForce/engagedSlabWidth=900 kN/6 m=150 kN/m. Excavation, structural work and backfilling have different load paths; the final model does not replace staged models. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]},{"id":"b166-v14-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「支撐拆換與荷載轉移」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Brace removal and load transfer\", which statement holds?","options":["道路恢復平整就表示全部地下工程已完成驗證","所有擋土牆都可以直接使用完全主動土壓","原創教學假設：transferredReaction=removedBraceForce/engagedSlabWidth=900 kN/6 m=150 kN/m。"],"optionsEn":["A smooth restored road proves all underground works have been verified","Every retaining wall can directly use fully active earth pressure","Original teaching assumptions: transferredReaction=removedBraceForce/engagedSlabWidth=900 kN/6 m=150 kN/m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：transferredReaction=removedBraceForce/engagedSlabWidth=900 kN/6 m=150 kN/m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: transferredReaction=removedBraceForce/engagedSlabWidth=900 kN/6 m=150 kN/m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b166-v14-27","title":"支撐拆換與荷載轉移：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Brace removal and load transfer: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"],"prerequisiteIds":["b166-v14-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「支撐拆換與荷載轉移」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Brace removal and load transfer” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"對照樓板成熟證據、接頭完成及拆換前後應變。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「接頭尚未傳力就拆支撐，牆移突增並使樓板邊緣開裂」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare slab maturity, joint completion and strains before and after load transfer. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: Removing a brace before joint engagement increases wall movement and cracks slab edges. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將對照樓板成熟證據、接頭完成及拆換前後應變列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現接頭尚未傳力就拆支撐，牆移突增並使樓板邊緣開裂，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","observationEn":"Site practice: Apply the following check at handover: Compare slab maturity, joint completion and strains before and after load transfer. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If removing a brace before joint engagement increases wall movement and cracks slab edges, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","failure":"注意干擾：接頭尚未傳力就拆支撐，牆移突增並使樓板邊緣開裂。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Removing a brace before joint engagement increases wall movement and cracks slab edges. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b166-v14-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"對照樓板成熟證據、接頭完成及拆換前後應變。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「接頭尚未傳力就拆支撐，牆移突增並使樓板邊緣開裂」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。","textEn":"Compare slab maturity, joint completion and strains before and after load transfer. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: Removing a brace before joint engagement increases wall movement and cracks slab edges. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]},{"id":"b166-v14-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將對照樓板成熟證據、接頭完成及拆換前後應變列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現接頭尚未傳力就拆支撐，牆移突增並使樓板邊緣開裂，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","textEn":"Apply the following check at handover: Compare slab maturity, joint completion and strains before and after load transfer. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If removing a brace before joint engagement increases wall movement and cracks slab edges, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「支撐拆換與荷載轉移」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Brace removal and load transfer\"?","options":["對照樓板成熟證據、接頭完成及拆換前後應變。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","基底往上動的所有原因都屬同一種失效"],"optionsEn":["Compare slab maturity, joint completion and strains before and after load transfer.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Every cause of upward base movement is the same failure mechanism"],"answer":0,"explanation":"對照樓板成熟證據、接頭完成及拆換前後應變。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare slab maturity, joint completion and strains before and after load transfer. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b166-v14-28","title":"支撐拆換與荷載轉移：失效診斷","titleEn":"Brace removal and load transfer: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"],"prerequisiteIds":["b166-v14-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「支撐拆換與荷載轉移」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Brace removal and load transfer” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"接頭尚未傳力就拆支撐，牆移突增並使樓板邊緣開裂。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到對照樓板成熟證據、接頭完成及拆換前後應變，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Removing a brace before joint engagement increases wall movement and cracks slab edges. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to compare slab maturity, joint completion and strains before and after load transfer to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：判別這個機制時，應觀察對照樓板成熟證據、接頭完成及拆換前後應變；若出現接頭尚未傳力就拆支撐，牆移突增並使樓板邊緣開裂，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: If removing a brace before joint engagement increases wall movement and cracks slab edges, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「永久樓板澆置完成就能立即取代全部臨時支撐」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A freshly cast permanent slab immediately replaces every temporary brace\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b166-v14-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"接頭尚未傳力就拆支撐，牆移突增並使樓板邊緣開裂。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到對照樓板成熟證據、接頭完成及拆換前後應變，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。","textEn":"Removing a brace before joint engagement increases wall movement and cracks slab edges. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to compare slab maturity, joint completion and strains before and after load transfer to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]},{"id":"b166-v14-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「支撐拆換與荷載轉移」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Brace removal and load transfer\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","接頭尚未傳力就拆支撐，牆移突增並使樓板邊緣開裂。","平均沉陷很小就代表鄰房一定沒有損傷"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Removing a brace before joint engagement increases wall movement and cracks slab edges.","Small average settlement guarantees no damage to neighbouring buildings"],"answer":1,"explanation":"接頭尚未傳力就拆支撐，牆移突增並使樓板邊緣開裂。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Removing a brace before joint engagement increases wall movement and cracks slab edges. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b166-v14-29","title":"鄰房沉陷與角變形：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Neighbour settlement and angular distortion: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"],"prerequisiteIds":["b166-v14-28"],"objective":"說明「鄰房沉陷與角變形」如何影響明挖覆蓋隧道施工的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Neighbour settlement and angular distortion” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Cut-and-cover tunnel construction”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"總沉陷與差異沉陷對建物的影響不同，剛體下沉可能不造成同樣裂縫，而局部角變形會擠壓門窗或拉開砌體。量測點需與建物結構分區相連，原有裂縫也應先記錄；不能把單一最大沉陷值當成全部損傷指標。 判別這個機制時，應觀察將建物水準、傾斜與原有裂縫圖按結構跨間比較；若出現平均沉陷小但局部差異大，砌體開裂被單一數值漏判，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「鄰房沉陷與角變形」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Total and differential settlements affect buildings differently: rigid movement can produce less cracking than local distortion. Connect survey points to structural divisions and document existing cracks. One maximum settlement value does not capture deformation patterns or establish damage causation by itself. Use the following check to discriminate the mechanism: Compare building levels, tilt and baseline cracks by structural bay. If small mean settlement hides local differential movement that cracks masonry, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Neighbour settlement and angular distortion” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：angularDistortion=settlementDifference/span=6 mm/12000 mm=0.0005。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: angularDistortion=settlementDifference/span=6 mm/12000 mm=0.0005.","failure":"常見誤解：「平均沉陷很小就代表鄰房一定沒有損傷」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Small average settlement guarantees no damage to neighbouring buildings\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「鄰房沉陷與角變形」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Neighbour settlement and angular distortion”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b166-v14-29-k1","title":"鄰房沉陷與角變形","titleEn":"Neighbour settlement and angular distortion","text":"總沉陷與差異沉陷對建物的影響不同，剛體下沉可能不造成同樣裂縫，而局部角變形會擠壓門窗或拉開砌體。量測點需與建物結構分區相連，原有裂縫也應先記錄；不能把單一最大沉陷值當成全部損傷指標。","textEn":"Total and differential settlements affect buildings differently: rigid movement can produce less cracking than local distortion. Connect survey points to structural divisions and document existing cracks.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]},{"id":"b166-v14-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：平均沉陷很小就代表鄰房一定沒有損傷 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Small average settlement guarantees no damage to neighbouring buildings Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「鄰房沉陷與角變形」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Neighbour settlement and angular distortion\" is correct?","options":["平均沉陷很小就代表鄰房一定沒有損傷","回填越快完成就能保證施工階段更安全","總沉陷與差異沉陷對建物的影響不同，剛體下沉可能不造成同樣裂縫，而局部角變形會擠壓門窗或拉開砌體。"],"optionsEn":["Small average settlement guarantees no damage to neighbouring buildings","Faster completion of backfilling guarantees safer construction stages","Total and differential settlements affect buildings differently: rigid movement can produce less cracking than local distortion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"總沉陷與差異沉陷對建物的影響不同，剛體下沉可能不造成同樣裂縫，而局部角變形會擠壓門窗或拉開砌體。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Total and differential settlements affect buildings differently: rigid movement can produce less cracking than local distortion. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b166-v14-30","title":"鄰房沉陷與角變形：定量估算","titleEn":"Neighbour settlement and angular distortion: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"],"prerequisiteIds":["b166-v14-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「鄰房沉陷與角變形」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Neighbour settlement and angular distortion” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：angularDistortion=settlementDifference/span=6 mm/12000 mm=0.0005。開挖、結構施工與回填具有不同荷載路徑，竣工模型不能取代施工模型。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: angularDistortion=settlementDifference/span=6 mm/12000 mm=0.0005. Excavation, structural work and backfilling have different load paths; the final model does not replace staged models. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將建物水準、傾斜與原有裂縫圖按結構跨間比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare building levels, tilt and baseline cracks by structural bay.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b166-v14-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：angularDistortion=settlementDifference/span=6 mm/12000 mm=0.0005。開挖、結構施工與回填具有不同荷載路徑，竣工模型不能取代施工模型。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: angularDistortion=settlementDifference/span=6 mm/12000 mm=0.0005. Excavation, structural work and backfilling have different load paths; the final model does not replace staged models. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]},{"id":"b166-v14-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「鄰房沉陷與角變形」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Neighbour settlement and angular distortion\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：angularDistortion=settlementDifference/span=6 mm/12000 mm=0.0005。","土方體積相同就代表兩個明挖工程風險相同","支撐荷重變大就只能是土壓增加"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: angularDistortion=settlementDifference/span=6 mm/12000 mm=0.0005.","Equal excavation volume means identical risk for two cut-and-cover projects","Increasing brace force can only mean increasing earth pressure"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：angularDistortion=settlementDifference/span=6 mm/12000 mm=0.0005。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: angularDistortion=settlementDifference/span=6 mm/12000 mm=0.0005. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b166-v14-31","title":"鄰房沉陷與角變形：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Neighbour settlement and angular distortion: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"],"prerequisiteIds":["b166-v14-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「鄰房沉陷與角變形」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Neighbour settlement and angular distortion” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將建物水準、傾斜與原有裂縫圖按結構跨間比較。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「平均沉陷小但局部差異大，砌體開裂被單一數值漏判」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare building levels, tilt and baseline cracks by structural bay. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: Small mean settlement hides local differential movement that cracks masonry. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將將建物水準、傾斜與原有裂縫圖按結構跨間比較列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現平均沉陷小但局部差異大，砌體開裂被單一數值漏判，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","observationEn":"Site practice: Apply the following check at handover: Compare building levels, tilt and baseline cracks by structural bay. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If small mean settlement hides local differential movement that cracks masonry, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","failure":"注意干擾：平均沉陷小但局部差異大，砌體開裂被單一數值漏判。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Small mean settlement hides local differential movement that cracks masonry. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b166-v14-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將建物水準、傾斜與原有裂縫圖按結構跨間比較。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「平均沉陷小但局部差異大，砌體開裂被單一數值漏判」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。","textEn":"Compare building levels, tilt and baseline cracks by structural bay. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: Small mean settlement hides local differential movement that cracks masonry. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]},{"id":"b166-v14-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將將建物水準、傾斜與原有裂縫圖按結構跨間比較列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現平均沉陷小但局部差異大，砌體開裂被單一數值漏判，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","textEn":"Apply the following check at handover: Compare building levels, tilt and baseline cracks by structural bay. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If small mean settlement hides local differential movement that cracks masonry, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「鄰房沉陷與角變形」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Neighbour settlement and angular distortion\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","將建物水準、傾斜與原有裂縫圖按結構跨間比較。","竣工抗浮合格就能保證每個施工階段都抗浮"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Compare building levels, tilt and baseline cracks by structural bay.","Passing permanent flotation checks guarantees every construction stage resists uplift"],"answer":1,"explanation":"將建物水準、傾斜與原有裂縫圖按結構跨間比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare building levels, tilt and baseline cracks by structural bay. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b166-v14-32","title":"鄰房沉陷與角變形：失效診斷","titleEn":"Neighbour settlement and angular distortion: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"],"prerequisiteIds":["b166-v14-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「鄰房沉陷與角變形」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Neighbour settlement and angular distortion” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"平均沉陷小但局部差異大，砌體開裂被單一數值漏判。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到將建物水準、傾斜與原有裂縫圖按結構跨間比較，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Small mean settlement hides local differential movement that cracks masonry. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to compare building levels, tilt and baseline cracks by structural bay to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：判別這個機制時，應觀察將建物水準、傾斜與原有裂縫圖按結構跨間比較；若出現平均沉陷小但局部差異大，砌體開裂被單一數值漏判，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: If small mean settlement hides local differential movement that cracks masonry, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「平均沉陷很小就代表鄰房一定沒有損傷」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Small average settlement guarantees no damage to neighbouring buildings\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b166-v14-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"平均沉陷小但局部差異大，砌體開裂被單一數值漏判。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到將建物水準、傾斜與原有裂縫圖按結構跨間比較，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。","textEn":"Small mean settlement hides local differential movement that cracks masonry. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to compare building levels, tilt and baseline cracks by structural bay to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]},{"id":"b166-v14-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「鄰房沉陷與角變形」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Neighbour settlement and angular distortion\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","回填越快完成就能保證施工階段更安全","平均沉陷小但局部差異大，砌體開裂被單一數值漏判。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Faster completion of backfilling guarantees safer construction stages","Small mean settlement hides local differential movement that cracks masonry."],"answer":2,"explanation":"平均沉陷小但局部差異大，砌體開裂被單一數值漏判。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Small mean settlement hides local differential movement that cracks masonry. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b166-v14-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「回填壓實與箱頂荷載」與「地表恢復與地下資產交接」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Backfill compaction and roof loading\" and \"Surface restoration and underground handover\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b166-v14-33","title":"回填壓實與箱頂荷載：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Backfill compaction and roof loading: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"],"prerequisiteIds":["b166-v14-32"],"objective":"說明「回填壓實與箱頂荷載」如何影響明挖覆蓋隧道施工的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Backfill compaction and roof loading” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Cut-and-cover tunnel construction”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"回填不只增加永久覆土，也會帶來施工機具與壓實作用；不對稱堆置可使箱體受扭或側壓不均。填料剛度與排水影響後續沉陷，不能只看壓實度數字；施工階段的機具位置和覆土厚度需要一起核對。 判別這個機制時，應觀察對照分層回填高程、機具位置及箱頂應變；若出現薄覆土上集中機具荷載讓箱頂局部超載，平均覆土帳未反映，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「回填壓實與箱頂荷載」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Backfill adds construction plant and compaction effects as well as permanent overburden; asymmetric placement changes lateral loading. Fill stiffness and drainage govern later settlement, beyond one density result. Check plant position and cover depth together when assessing temporary roof demand. Use the following check to discriminate the mechanism: Compare lift levels, equipment locations and roof strains. If concentrated plant above thin cover overloads the roof despite acceptable average fill, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Backfill compaction and roof loading” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：overburdenPressure=unitWeight*depth=20 kN/m3*2 m=40 kPa。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: overburdenPressure=unitWeight*depth=20 kN/m3*2 m=40 kPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「回填越快完成就能保證施工階段更安全」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Faster completion of backfilling guarantees safer construction stages\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「回填壓實與箱頂荷載」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Backfill compaction and roof loading”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b166-v14-33-k1","title":"回填壓實與箱頂荷載","titleEn":"Backfill compaction and roof loading","text":"回填不只增加永久覆土，也會帶來施工機具與壓實作用；不對稱堆置可使箱體受扭或側壓不均。填料剛度與排水影響後續沉陷，不能只看壓實度數字；施工階段的機具位置和覆土厚度需要一起核對。","textEn":"Backfill adds construction plant and compaction effects as well as permanent overburden; asymmetric placement changes lateral loading. Fill stiffness and drainage govern later settlement, beyond one density result.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]},{"id":"b166-v14-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：回填越快完成就能保證施工階段更安全 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Faster completion of backfilling guarantees safer construction stages Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「回填壓實與箱頂荷載」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Backfill compaction and roof loading\" is correct?","options":["回填不只增加永久覆土，也會帶來施工機具與壓實作用；不對稱堆置可使箱體受扭或側壓不均。","回填越快完成就能保證施工階段更安全","道路恢復平整就表示全部地下工程已完成驗證"],"optionsEn":["Backfill adds construction plant and compaction effects as well as permanent overburden; asymmetric placement changes lateral loading.","Faster completion of backfilling guarantees safer construction stages","A smooth restored road proves all underground works have been verified"],"answer":0,"explanation":"回填不只增加永久覆土，也會帶來施工機具與壓實作用；不對稱堆置可使箱體受扭或側壓不均。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Backfill adds construction plant and compaction effects as well as permanent overburden; asymmetric placement changes lateral loading. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b166-v14-34","title":"回填壓實與箱頂荷載：定量估算","titleEn":"Backfill compaction and roof loading: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"],"prerequisiteIds":["b166-v14-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「回填壓實與箱頂荷載」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Backfill compaction and roof loading” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：overburdenPressure=unitWeight*depth=20 kN/m3*2 m=40 kPa。開挖、結構施工與回填具有不同荷載路徑，竣工模型不能取代施工模型。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: overburdenPressure=unitWeight*depth=20 kN/m3*2 m=40 kPa. Excavation, structural work and backfilling have different load paths; the final model does not replace staged models. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：對照分層回填高程、機具位置及箱頂應變。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare lift levels, equipment locations and roof strains.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b166-v14-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：overburdenPressure=unitWeight*depth=20 kN/m3*2 m=40 kPa。開挖、結構施工與回填具有不同荷載路徑，竣工模型不能取代施工模型。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: overburdenPressure=unitWeight*depth=20 kN/m3*2 m=40 kPa. Excavation, structural work and backfilling have different load paths; the final model does not replace staged models. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]},{"id":"b166-v14-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「回填壓實與箱頂荷載」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Backfill compaction and roof loading\", which statement holds?","options":["所有擋土牆都可以直接使用完全主動土壓","原創教學假設：overburdenPressure=unitWeight*depth=20 kN/m3*2 m=40 kPa。","基底往上動的所有原因都屬同一種失效"],"optionsEn":["Every retaining wall can directly use fully active earth pressure","Original teaching assumptions: overburdenPressure=unitWeight*depth=20 kN/m3*2 m=40 kPa.","Every cause of upward base movement is the same failure mechanism"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：overburdenPressure=unitWeight*depth=20 kN/m3*2 m=40 kPa。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: overburdenPressure=unitWeight*depth=20 kN/m3*2 m=40 kPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b166-v14-35","title":"回填壓實與箱頂荷載：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Backfill compaction and roof loading: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"],"prerequisiteIds":["b166-v14-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「回填壓實與箱頂荷載」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Backfill compaction and roof loading” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"對照分層回填高程、機具位置及箱頂應變。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「薄覆土上集中機具荷載讓箱頂局部超載，平均覆土帳未反映」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare lift levels, equipment locations and roof strains. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: Concentrated plant above thin cover overloads the roof despite acceptable average fill. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將對照分層回填高程、機具位置及箱頂應變列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現薄覆土上集中機具荷載讓箱頂局部超載，平均覆土帳未反映，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","observationEn":"Site practice: Apply the following check at handover: Compare lift levels, equipment locations and roof strains. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If concentrated plant above thin cover overloads the roof despite acceptable average fill, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","failure":"注意干擾：薄覆土上集中機具荷載讓箱頂局部超載，平均覆土帳未反映。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Concentrated plant above thin cover overloads the roof despite acceptable average fill. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b166-v14-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"對照分層回填高程、機具位置及箱頂應變。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「薄覆土上集中機具荷載讓箱頂局部超載，平均覆土帳未反映」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。","textEn":"Compare lift levels, equipment locations and roof strains. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: Concentrated plant above thin cover overloads the roof despite acceptable average fill. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]},{"id":"b166-v14-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將對照分層回填高程、機具位置及箱頂應變列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現薄覆土上集中機具荷載讓箱頂局部超載，平均覆土帳未反映，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","textEn":"Apply the following check at handover: Compare lift levels, equipment locations and roof strains. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If concentrated plant above thin cover overloads the roof despite acceptable average fill, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「回填壓實與箱頂荷載」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Backfill compaction and roof loading\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","箱體牆面不裂就能保證所有穿牆位置都不漏","對照分層回填高程、機具位置及箱頂應變。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Uncracked box walls guarantee every penetration remains watertight","Compare lift levels, equipment locations and roof strains."],"answer":2,"explanation":"對照分層回填高程、機具位置及箱頂應變。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare lift levels, equipment locations and roof strains. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b166-v14-36","title":"回填壓實與箱頂荷載：失效診斷","titleEn":"Backfill compaction and roof loading: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"],"prerequisiteIds":["b166-v14-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「回填壓實與箱頂荷載」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Backfill compaction and roof loading” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"薄覆土上集中機具荷載讓箱頂局部超載，平均覆土帳未反映。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到對照分層回填高程、機具位置及箱頂應變，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Concentrated plant above thin cover overloads the roof despite acceptable average fill. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to compare lift levels, equipment locations and roof strains to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：判別這個機制時，應觀察對照分層回填高程、機具位置及箱頂應變；若出現薄覆土上集中機具荷載讓箱頂局部超載，平均覆土帳未反映，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: If concentrated plant above thin cover overloads the roof despite acceptable average fill, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「回填越快完成就能保證施工階段更安全」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Faster completion of backfilling guarantees safer construction stages\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b166-v14-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"薄覆土上集中機具荷載讓箱頂局部超載，平均覆土帳未反映。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到對照分層回填高程、機具位置及箱頂應變，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。","textEn":"Concentrated plant above thin cover overloads the roof despite acceptable average fill. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to compare lift levels, equipment locations and roof strains to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]},{"id":"b166-v14-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「回填壓實與箱頂荷載」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Backfill compaction and roof loading\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["薄覆土上集中機具荷載讓箱頂局部超載，平均覆土帳未反映。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","道路恢復平整就表示全部地下工程已完成驗證"],"optionsEn":["Concentrated plant above thin cover overloads the roof despite acceptable average fill.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","A smooth restored road proves all underground works have been verified"],"answer":0,"explanation":"薄覆土上集中機具荷載讓箱頂局部超載，平均覆土帳未反映。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Concentrated plant above thin cover overloads the roof despite acceptable average fill. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b166-v14-37","title":"地表恢復與地下資產交接：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Surface restoration and underground handover: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"],"prerequisiteIds":["b166-v14-36"],"objective":"說明「地表恢復與地下資產交接」如何影響明挖覆蓋隧道施工的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Surface restoration and underground handover” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Cut-and-cover tunnel construction”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"道路恢復後，地下接縫、排水和檢查孔可能變得難以接近，維護動線須在交接時確認。竣工圖應記錄實際高程與管線改道，不能只保留原設計；地表平順也不能證明回填長期不沉陷，需建立後續比較基準。 判別這個機制時，應觀察核對竣工管線、檢查通道及道路沉陷基準點；若出現維修口被道路設施遮住，使早期堵塞無法檢查清理，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「地表恢復與地下資產交接」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"After road restoration, joints, drains and access points become harder to reach, making maintenance access part of handover. Record as-built levels and utility diversions rather than design alone. A smooth surface does not establish long-term fill stability, so retain a postconstruction baseline. Use the following check to discriminate the mechanism: Audit as-built utilities, inspection access and road-settlement reference points. If road installations conceal maintenance openings and prevent early blockage inspection, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Surface restoration and underground handover” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：Inputs independent component standard uncertainties=0.01,0.02,0.02 m; surveyClosure=sqrt(0.01^2+0.02^2+0.02^2)=0.03 m for assumed independent components。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Inputs independent component standard uncertainties=0.01,0.02,0.02 m; surveyClosure=sqrt(0.01^2+0.02^2+0.02^2)=0.03 m for assumed independent components.","failure":"常見誤解：「道路恢復平整就表示全部地下工程已完成驗證」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A smooth restored road proves all underground works have been verified\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「地表恢復與地下資產交接」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Surface restoration and underground handover”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b166-v14-37-k1","title":"地表恢復與地下資產交接","titleEn":"Surface restoration and underground handover","text":"道路恢復後，地下接縫、排水和檢查孔可能變得難以接近，維護動線須在交接時確認。竣工圖應記錄實際高程與管線改道，不能只保留原設計；地表平順也不能證明回填長期不沉陷，需建立後續比較基準。","textEn":"After road restoration, joints, drains and access points become harder to reach, making maintenance access part of handover. Record as-built levels and utility diversions rather than design alone.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]},{"id":"b166-v14-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：道路恢復平整就表示全部地下工程已完成驗證 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A smooth restored road proves all underground works have been verified Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「地表恢復與地下資產交接」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Surface restoration and underground handover\" is correct?","options":["道路恢復平整就表示全部地下工程已完成驗證","道路恢復後，地下接縫、排水和檢查孔可能變得難以接近，維護動線須在交接時確認。","土方體積相同就代表兩個明挖工程風險相同"],"optionsEn":["A smooth restored road proves all underground works have been verified","After road restoration, joints, drains and access points become harder to reach, making maintenance access part of handover.","Equal excavation volume means identical risk for two cut-and-cover projects"],"answer":1,"explanation":"道路恢復後，地下接縫、排水和檢查孔可能變得難以接近，維護動線須在交接時確認。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"After road restoration, joints, drains and access points become harder to reach, making maintenance access part of handover. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b166-v14-38","title":"地表恢復與地下資產交接：定量估算","titleEn":"Surface restoration and underground handover: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"],"prerequisiteIds":["b166-v14-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「地表恢復與地下資產交接」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Surface restoration and underground handover” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：Inputs independent component standard uncertainties=0.01,0.02,0.02 m; surveyClosure=sqrt(0.01^2+0.02^2+0.02^2)=0.03 m for assumed independent components。開挖、結構施工與回填具有不同荷載路徑，竣工模型不能取代施工模型。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: Inputs independent component standard uncertainties=0.01,0.02,0.02 m; surveyClosure=sqrt(0.01^2+0.02^2+0.02^2)=0.03 m for assumed independent components. Excavation, structural work and backfilling have different load paths; the final model does not replace staged models. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對竣工管線、檢查通道及道路沉陷基準點。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Audit as-built utilities, inspection access and road-settlement reference points.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b166-v14-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：Inputs independent component standard uncertainties=0.01,0.02,0.02 m; surveyClosure=sqrt(0.01^2+0.02^2+0.02^2)=0.03 m for assumed independent components。開挖、結構施工與回填具有不同荷載路徑，竣工模型不能取代施工模型。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Inputs independent component standard uncertainties=0.01,0.02,0.02 m; surveyClosure=sqrt(0.01^2+0.02^2+0.02^2)=0.03 m for assumed independent components. Excavation, structural work and backfilling have different load paths; the final model does not replace staged models. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]},{"id":"b166-v14-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「地表恢復與地下資產交接」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Surface restoration and underground handover\", which statement holds?","options":["支撐荷重變大就只能是土壓增加","竣工抗浮合格就能保證每個施工階段都抗浮","原創教學假設：Inputs independent component standard uncertainties=0.01,0.02,0.02 m; surveyClosure=sqrt(0.01^2+0.02^2+0.02^2)=0.03 m for assumed independent components。"],"optionsEn":["Increasing brace force can only mean increasing earth pressure","Passing permanent flotation checks guarantees every construction stage resists uplift","Original teaching assumptions: Inputs independent component standard uncertainties=0.01,0.02,0.02 m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：Inputs independent component standard uncertainties=0.01,0.02,0.02 m; surveyClosure=sqrt(0.01^2+0.02^2+0.02^2)=0.03 m for assumed independent components。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Inputs independent component standard uncertainties=0.01,0.02,0.02 m; surveyClosure=sqrt(0.01^2+0.02^2+0.02^2)=0.03 m for assumed independent components. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b166-v14-39","title":"地表恢復與地下資產交接：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Surface restoration and underground handover: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"],"prerequisiteIds":["b166-v14-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「地表恢復與地下資產交接」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Surface restoration and underground handover” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對竣工管線、檢查通道及道路沉陷基準點。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「維修口被道路設施遮住，使早期堵塞無法檢查清理」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Audit as-built utilities, inspection access and road-settlement reference points. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: Road installations conceal maintenance openings and prevent early blockage inspection. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將核對竣工管線、檢查通道及道路沉陷基準點列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現維修口被道路設施遮住，使早期堵塞無法檢查清理，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","observationEn":"Site practice: Apply the following check at handover: Audit as-built utilities, inspection access and road-settlement reference points. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If road installations conceal maintenance openings and prevent early blockage inspection, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","failure":"注意干擾：維修口被道路設施遮住，使早期堵塞無法檢查清理。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Road installations conceal maintenance openings and prevent early blockage inspection. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b166-v14-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對竣工管線、檢查通道及道路沉陷基準點。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「維修口被道路設施遮住，使早期堵塞無法檢查清理」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。","textEn":"Audit as-built utilities, inspection access and road-settlement reference points. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: Road installations conceal maintenance openings and prevent early blockage inspection. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]},{"id":"b166-v14-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將核對竣工管線、檢查通道及道路沉陷基準點列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現維修口被道路設施遮住，使早期堵塞無法檢查清理，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","textEn":"Apply the following check at handover: Audit as-built utilities, inspection access and road-settlement reference points. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If road installations conceal maintenance openings and prevent early blockage inspection, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「地表恢復與地下資產交接」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Surface restoration and underground handover\"?","options":["核對竣工管線、檢查通道及道路沉陷基準點。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","永久樓板澆置完成就能立即取代全部臨時支撐"],"optionsEn":["Audit as-built utilities, inspection access and road-settlement reference points.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","A freshly cast permanent slab immediately replaces every temporary brace"],"answer":0,"explanation":"核對竣工管線、檢查通道及道路沉陷基準點。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Audit as-built utilities, inspection access and road-settlement reference points. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b166-v14-40","title":"地表恢復與地下資產交接：失效診斷","titleEn":"Surface restoration and underground handover: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"],"prerequisiteIds":["b166-v14-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「地表恢復與地下資產交接」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Surface restoration and underground handover” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"維修口被道路設施遮住，使早期堵塞無法檢查清理。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到核對竣工管線、檢查通道及道路沉陷基準點，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Road installations conceal maintenance openings and prevent early blockage inspection. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to audit as-built utilities, inspection access and road-settlement reference points to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：判別這個機制時，應觀察核對竣工管線、檢查通道及道路沉陷基準點；若出現維修口被道路設施遮住，使早期堵塞無法檢查清理，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: If road installations conceal maintenance openings and prevent early blockage inspection, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「道路恢復平整就表示全部地下工程已完成驗證」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A smooth restored road proves all underground works have been verified\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b166-v14-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"維修口被道路設施遮住，使早期堵塞無法檢查清理。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到核對竣工管線、檢查通道及道路沉陷基準點，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。","textEn":"Road installations conceal maintenance openings and prevent early blockage inspection. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to audit as-built utilities, inspection access and road-settlement reference points to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]},{"id":"b166-v14-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「地表恢復與地下資產交接」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Surface restoration and underground handover\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","維修口被道路設施遮住，使早期堵塞無法檢查清理。","土方體積相同就代表兩個明挖工程風險相同"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Road installations conceal maintenance openings and prevent early blockage inspection.","Equal excavation volume means identical risk for two cut-and-cover projects"],"answer":1,"explanation":"維修口被道路設施遮住，使早期堵塞無法檢查清理。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Road installations conceal maintenance openings and prevent early blockage inspection. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-paddington","v14s-big-dig"],"curriculumVersion":14,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
